module_specs:
  clock_gen: |
    Generate a nominal 74.25 MHz pixel clock from the 100 MHz board clock and expose the clock generator lock indication. With SIM_DIRECT_CLOCK=0, generate pix_clk from the 100 MHz clock using an MMCM; with SIM_DIRECT_CLOCK=1, use the clock input directly as the pixel clock.
  raster_source: |
    Generate the complete 1650-clock by 750-line raster with 1280 by 720 active pixels, positive syncs, and the specified porches. Pattern select 0 produces the specified colour bars; pattern select 1 produces a checkerboard. Emit one stream beat for every raster pixel clock, carrying RGB plus active, hsync, and vsync metadata. Increment the 32-bit frame counter once per completed frame; reset it to zero and allow natural unsigned wraparound.
  median_filter: |
    For each active output pixel and each RGB channel, calculate the median of that channel's 3 x 3 active-picture neighbourhood. Replicate the nearest active-edge pixel when the neighbourhood extends beyond the active picture. Preserve raster metadata and align the filtered picture with its sync signals. Do not stall the raster stream. Produce one output beat per input beat at one beat per clock, with one clock cycle latency.
  video_output: |
    Drive VGA sync from the stream metadata and drive the four-bit RGB channels from the filtered pixel data. Drive RGB to zero outside the active picture, while the synchronized centre button is pressed, or while the synchronized clock-stable indication is false. Keep sync outputs aligned with the pixel stream.

requirements:
  - id: S-1
    text: "Generate VGA timing at 1280 x 720 active pixels and 60 Hz using a nominal 74.25 MHz pixel clock, 1650 pixel clocks per line (1280 active, 110 front porch, 40 sync, 220 back porch), and 750 lines per frame (720 active, 5 front porch, 5 sync, 20 back porch), with positive horizontal and vertical sync."
    proof: [simulation, hardware, analysis]
    modules: [clock_gen, raster_source, video_output, top]
  - id: S-2
    text: "With the default pattern selected, display eight vertical bars, each 160 active pixels wide, in this order: white, yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, blue, black."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [raster_source, video_output, top]
  - id: S-3
    text: "For each output pixel and each colour channel, produce the median of that channel's nine samples in the corresponding 3 x 3 input neighbourhood."
    proof: [simulation, formal]
    modules: [median_filter]
  - id: S-4
    text: "Keep the filtered picture aligned with the VGA sync signals so that filtering does not shift the picture's active region relative to the specified video timing."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [raster_source, median_filter, video_output]
  - id: S-5
    text: "Drive all colour outputs to zero outside the active picture, while BTNC is pressed, or while the pixel clock is not stable."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_output, top]
  - id: S-6
    text: "Illuminate LED[0] when the pixel clock is stable and leave it unilluminated when the pixel clock is not stable."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [clock_gen, top]
  - id: S-7
    text: "Provide a USB-UART test shell operating at 115200 baud that identifies the design as VMED, allows the host to select a test pattern, and allows the host to read a frame counter."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [raster_source, top]

